        244
      ],
      "sourceURL": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikisource/he/e/ed/Apocrypha_Kahana_A2.pdf#page=244",
      "decision": "retainUnresolvedSourceNote",
      "finding": "The complete initial vav has a broad lower mass fused directly to the stem, with a flat lower edge and no surviving separate boundary between letter foot and point. The same-page initial vav in ויסגרו has a similar mass. The literal yod patah of ויחתמו is a separate horizontal mass, the yod hiriq of ויסגרו is round, and the tav qamats in אוֹתָהּ has a transverse head and tail. The target has absorbed the upper boundary needed to decide whether its broadened foot is a fused bar, a broadened single point, or another damaged shape. A likely reading is not sufficient; keep the first-vav vowel omission.",
      "baselinePhysicalAnnotationSpan": [
        0,
        8
      ],
      "targetFrame": "target01-initial-vav",
      "wordFrame": "target-word-vayomru",
      "controlFrames": [
        "control-vayisgeru-initial-vav",
        "control-vayichtemu-word",
        "control-vayisgeru-yod-dagesh-hiriq",
        "control-otah-tav-qamats"
      ]
    },
    {
      "book": "BEL",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 12,
      "id": "bel-1-12-244-vayomru12-letter2-dagesh",
      "kind": "unreadablePoint",
      "anchor": "ויֹאמְרו",
      "occurrence": 1,
      "letterIndex": 2,
      "mark": "dagesh",
      "sourcePages": [
        244
      ],
      "sourceURL": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikisource/he/e/ed/Apocrypha_Kahana_A2.pdf#page=244",
      "decision": "retainUnresolvedSourceNote",
      "finding": "The complete yod retains the existing holam above. Its lower-left body forms a shallow cleft and broad lobe, unlike the slimmer ordinary final yod of כֹּהֲנֵי, but the entire lobe is consumed by the enlarged head/stem silhouette. The literal dotted yod in ויסגרו demonstrates the relevant lower-left dot position, yet the target does not preserve a distinctive round dot shoulder that securely excludes spread of the body. Neither dot nor source absence is certified. Keep the yod dagesh omission and preserve the holam scalar/order.",
      "baselinePhysicalAnnotationSpan": [
        0,
        8
      ],
      "targetFrame": "target02-yod",
      "wordFrame": "target-word-vayomru",
      "controlFrames": [
        "control-vayisgeru-yod-dagesh-hiriq",
        "control-kohanei-yod-without-dot"
      ]
    },
    {
      "book": "BEL",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 12,
      "id": "bel-1-12-244-vayomru12-letter6-dagesh",
      "kind": "unreadablePoint",
      "anchor": "ויֹאמְרו",
      "occurrence": 1,
      "letterIndex": 6,
      "mark": "dagesh",
      "sourcePages": [
        244
      ],
      "sourceURL": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikisource/he/e/ed/Apocrypha_Kahana_A2.pdf#page=244",
      "decision": "proposeSourceCertifiedPoint",
      "finding": "The final vav retains a distinct rounded lower-left lobe below its main head. A narrow neck joins the lobe to the head, and its right side meets the stem while the contour re-expands into the rounded left point; the long right stem continues well below it. This matches the literal final-vav dot in אנחנו and the final-vav dot in ויסגרו. The full holam-bearing vav of אוֹתָהּ has the same descending head/stem pattern but no left lobe. The whole contour, including the exposed point shoulder and its position below the head, distinguishes the target from ordinary stem thickening. Propose exactly U+05BC on final vav; preserve the existing legacy dagesh note category until retiring that note. No grammatical expectation supplies the point.",
      "baselinePhysicalAnnotationSpan": [
        0,
        8
      ],
      "targetFrame": "target03-final-vav",
      "wordFrame": "target-word-vayomru",
      "controlFrames": [
        "control-anachnu-final-vav-dot",
        "control-vayisgeru-word",
        "control-otah-vav-without-dot"
      ]
    }
